    "model_resolution": "prose-repository-mentioned",
    "observed_command": "<@394912327109050378> I have installed your quant - thank you for that! rapid response! I have the following problem: when the model copies data from tool output, sometimes it does little mistakes (1 out of 50). In one of my tests it had to copy 100 email addresses. In 5 of them it did the following errors at the email addresses: 1. `ashad@...` became `cashad@...` 2. `cerig@...` became `ccerig@...` 3. `carlos@...` became `ccarlos@...` 4. `jens@...` became `jjens@...` 5. `paterson@...` became `person@...` I run it with `vllm-0.19.0` like this: ``` export VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_MOE_FP4=1 export VLLM_FLASHINFER_MOE_BACKEND=throughput export VLLM_WORKER_MULTIPROC_METHOD=spawn export NVIDIA_TF32_OVERRIDE=1 export VLLM_FLOAT32_MATMUL_PRECISION=high export NCCL_ALGO=Ring export NCCL_PROTO=Simple export NCCL_MIN_NCHANNELS=8 export NCCL_MAX_NCHANNELS=16 export NCCL_BUFFSIZE=16777216 export NCCL_P2P_DISABLE=0 export NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1 export NCCL_NVLS_ENABLE=0 export NCCL_SHM_DISABLE=0 export PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True,max_split_size_mb:512 export VLLM_MEMORY_PROFILER_ESTIMATE_CUDAGRAPHS=1 SAMPLER_OVERRIDE='{\"temperature\": 1, \"top_p\": 0.95, \"top_k\": 40, \"repetition_penalty\": 1.1, \"frequency_penalty\": 0.40}' exec vllm serve lukealonso/MiniMax-M2.7-NVFP4 --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8357 --served-model-name minimax-m2.7 --trust-remote-code --gpu-memory-utilization 0.9419 --tensor-parallel-size 2 --pipeline-parallel-size 1 --max-model-len 196608 --max-num-seqs 16 --max-num-batc",
